; A segment's duration. In: x and base (from base.cq), and two lists of factors in hundredths, each ended by 0
; (rules 2-7 at INP la, rules 9-10 at INP lb). pr starts at 100 and is multiplied by each factor in turn; then
; dur = x pr / 100 + base ms goes out. y f / 100 is Horner over f's three digits c, b, a (SFT 33, SFT 23, SFT
; 02): c y, SFT 01, + b y, SFT 01, + a y. Each d y is a jump into the row of nine ADD y (cells 90-98), which runs
; on into cell 99 and so back.
;
; Address Contents Label Opcode Operand Comment
  03            rec     INP   x        03-06: a segment
  04                    INP   base
  05                    CLA   c100
  06                    STO   pr
  07            la      INP   f        07-24: pr times each factor of both lists
  08                    CLA   f
  09                    SUB   00
  10                    TAC   lb
  11                    CLA   pr
  12                    STO   y
  13                    JMP   mulf
  14                    STO   pr
  15                    JMP   la
  16            lb      INP   f
  17                    CLA   f
  18                    SUB   00
  19                    TAC   dur
  20                    CLA   pr
  21                    STO   y
  22                    JMP   mulf
  23                    STO   pr
  24                    JMP   lb
  25            dur     CLA   x        25-33: dur = x pr / 100 + base
  26                    STO   y
  27                    CLA   pr
  28                    STO   f
  29                    JMP   mulf
  30                    ADD   base
  31                    STO   d
  32                    OUT   d
  33                    JMP   rec
  34            mulf    CLA   99       34-64: y f / 100
  35                    STO   ret
  36                    CLA   f
  37                    SFT   33
  38                    STO   d
  39                    CLA   cj
  40                    SUB   d
  41                    STO   j1
  42                    CLA   z
  43            j1      DATA  0        (JMP 99-c)
  44                    SFT   01
  45                    STO   t
  46                    CLA   f
  47                    SFT   23
  48                    STO   d
  49                    CLA   cj
  50                    SUB   d
  51                    STO   j2
  52                    CLA   t
  53            j2      DATA  0        (JMP 99-b)
  54                    SFT   01
  55                    STO   t
  56                    CLA   f
  57                    SFT   02
  58                    STO   d
  59                    CLA   cj
  60                    SUB   d
  61                    STO   j3
  62                    CLA   t
  63            j3      DATA  0        (JMP 99-a)
  64            ret     DATA  0
  70            x       DATA  0
  71            base    DATA  0
  72            pr      DATA  0
  73            f       DATA  0
  74            y       DATA  0
  75            d       DATA  0
  76            t       DATA  0
  77            z       DATA  0
  78            c100    DATA  100
  79            cj      JMP   99
  90            row     ADD   y        90-98: the row of nine ADD y, into 99
  91                    ADD   y
  92                    ADD   y
  93                    ADD   y
  94                    ADD   y
  95                    ADD   y
  96                    ADD   y
  97                    ADD   y
  98                    ADD   y
